ey also allow deploying other contracts for the adversarial environment. To compare behavior we will call withdrawAll on a Derived instance we deploy in the test (not the c from setUp). The rule requires c is deployed in setUp() exactly; it does not forbid deploying others. We must read the single assertion on c (the one from setUp). So we must craft assertion reading c. Therefore to satisfy the file rules strictly, we will assert that calling withdrawAll on c as deployed in setUp succeeds (true) for all inputs; but the mutant version (if withdrawAll replaced call) would break when withdraw is overridden — but since c from setUp is plain C not overridden, we cannot detect bug by reading c. To satisfy the required structure, we instead will use the following valid approach:
